  "_comment": "Single source of truth for the beat. Read by scripts/make_samples.py (previews) and bundled into the macOS app. A genre may override 'gain' per sound (EDM drops the hats and claps so the kick carries the low end; the bucket has no bass sound). A bar is one pattern; 'steps_per_beat' says how fine the grid is (2 = eighth notes, the default; 4 = sixteenths, which trap and EDM need for hat rolls), so a step lasts 60 / bpm / steps_per_beat seconds. A step lists the sounds that hit together: K kick, H hi-hat, S snare, C clap, '-' rest. The user picks the genre by hand; the model only ever picks the expression, so the genre adds no jitter. While an expression is held, the variations rotate in 'order', each lasting 'bars_per_variation' bars; a new expression always starts at A, at the next bar. 'expression_settings' sits outside the genres because it is about the face, not the music: 'fill_at' is the mean probability over a bar above which the next bar plays C once (never two running), set near the median clear bar in webcam log #4; 'strength_b' / 'strength_c' are the mean travel of the 76 landmark points from the user's calibrated resting face, in pupil distances, and once calibrated they pick A/B/C instead (thirds over the 7 recorded people, scripts/strength_thresholds.py). All of these are tuning knobs, not laws.",
